  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A small demonstration corner can host one optional technique lesson each week without blocking ordinary bench use.\", \"decision\": \"How should a short technique demonstration be selected?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers propose techniques on the board and vote before the steward arranges the weekly demonstration. The lesson follows expressed interest, giving members a direct role in choosing what they can learn together.\nThe steward chooses a weekly technique from recurring help requests and invites members to the demonstration corner. Questions already interrupting projects become the basis for a shared lesson that may prevent repeated consultations.\nMembers volunteer to demonstrate techniques they know, and the steward schedules the offers in a rotating order. The lesson program grows from available member expertise while different volunteers receive opportunities to contribute."
    }
  ],
